<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Bottom-nav surface, shared by all five tab screens.

    Deliberately a flat fill with NO top border. It carried a 1dp hairline
    (wedora_hairline, the board's rgba(255,255,255,0.1) from Figma 118:506 /
    118:537) until that line was judged too visible in use.

    The consequence is intended, not overlooked: wedora_nav_bg and wedora_bg are
    the same #120D12 in dark, so the bar has no boundary against the page at
    all, and content scrolls up to it with nothing marking where it begins. If a
    separation is ever wanted back, shifting wedora_nav_bg is the lever - not
    reinstating a rule.

    Both tokens resolve to existing light values in light mode and to the
    board's in dark, so this restyles dark without touching light, which has no
    design to restyle toward.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/wedora_nav_bg" />
</shape>
